title: Jefferson Davis Treason Case
subtitle: The Rebel Leader on Trial
tags: event
view-if: year = 1866 and month >= 6
max-visits: 1

= Jefferson Davis Treason Case

Jefferson Davis remains under arrest for his leadership of the rebellious Confederate states. <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> push for a high-profile treason trial, seeing it as essential to uphold federal authority. <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderates**</span> and <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservatives**</span> warn that such a trial could spark Southern vengeance or risk a Supreme Court ruling that legitimizes secession.

Do we proceed with prosecuting Davis?

- @CONVICT: Pursue the treason trial
- @NOPE: Avoid the trial

@CONVICT
subtitle: Take the risk, try him in court
choose-if: rep_majority >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [if rep_majority < 1: We don't have a majority]
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/Jeff.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

on-arrival: radical_strength += 1; radical_dissent -= 2; moderate_strength -= 1; conservative_strength -= 2; conservative_dissent += 2; kkk_strength += 5; kkk_militancy += 0.1;

Congress votes to put Davis on trial. <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> celebrate a stand for the Republic, while <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderates**</span> and <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservatives**</span> warn of the dangers: Southern resentment may explode, and a hostile court could even declare secession legal, threatening the legitimacy of Reconstruction.

@NOPE
subtitle: Exercise caution, avoid provocation
on-arrival: radical_strength -= 1; radical_dissent += 2; moderate_strength += 2; conservative_strength += 2; conservative_dissent -= 2; kkk_strength -= 3; kkk_militancy -= 0.1;

<span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderate**</span> and <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservative**</span> voices prevail. They cite Lincoln's approach of forgiveness and argue that a trial could validate Redeemer propaganda in the South. Avoiding the trial maintains relative stability but frustrates the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span>, who see an opportunity for federal authority lost.